# Everything here is Trilium's source except data/, and DVC walks whatever it
# is not told to skip. node_modules alone is ~100k files, so an unfiltered
# `dvc status` costs minutes on a worktree that pins two directories.
#
# live/ is listed for a second reason: the database and its write-ahead log are
# one unit, so a pin taken while the server runs records a state that never
# existed. Nothing must make it reachable by accident.
/apps/
/docs/
/live/
/node_modules/
/packages/
/patches/
/scripts/
